import sys
p = sys.argv[1]
lines = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read().split('\n')
idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('| 598 |')]
assert len(idx) == 1
lines.insert(idx[0] + 1, "| 599 | 2026-10-21 | **Old Scales tools that the eleven lessons now cover are removed.** Her call: overlapping tools go unless they have a special function. Removed from the Toolbox registry, Korean strings, badge art, tool maps, related-tool pairs and the Scales chapter list: `ssc-steps`, `ssc-fingers`, `ssc-degrees`, `ssc-g`, `ssc-f` (covered by lessons 1–5 and the ▶ up and down), `major-shape` and `build-major` (lessons 1–2, 9), `degree-names` (lesson 3), `minor-forms` (lesson 11). Kept because they do something the lessons do not: `scale-finder` (to be reborn), `major-fingering` and `minor-fingering` (the \"scale path\" and the minor fingerings), `build-minor` (any minor, not only D), `modes`, `chromatic` and `tone-semitone` (enharmonic names; belong to the accidentals chapter). The old Scales concept book page \"Every key\" now embeds the lesson 9 tool (`sc-all`) instead of `build-major`; the chapter default tool for Scales is `scale-finder`. The component code (`SscPad`, `MajorShapeCard`, `ScaleBuilder`, `MinorFormsCard` and others) is left in the file because the old \"Learn the whole chapter\" page still uses it; it goes when the chapters are rebuilt. Built by `patch608.py` (`t612`). Checked 16 routes before and after (Toolbox, Scales chapter, drill, concept book in English and Korean, the removed ids): no console errors; a removed id now shows the Toolbox page. Local commit only, not pushed. |")
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write('\n'.join(lines)); print('ok')
